<interrogationes unitas="pictor_applicatio">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I start the pictor drawing app from a new main, window or terminal?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_volumen_aperire pictor_applicatio_aedificare PictorApplicatio" via="apps/pictor/pictor.c apps/pictor/pictor_terminalis.c">Call
      thema_initiare yourself (glue's job), open the volume with
      pictor_volumen_aperire(piscina, argc, argv, &amp;fumus) (-fumus =
      temporary volume, -volumen PATH, default "pictor.volumen"), then
      pictor_applicatio_aedificare with the surface size in our
      pixels. Hand app.d, app.figurae and &amp;app.montatio.figurae_ctx
      to your glue (ludus_fenestra or ludus_tessera).
      pictor_volumen_aperire returns NIHIL if the volume cannot be
      opened; pictor_applicatio_aedificare returns FALSUM if any part
      (repository, mount, dispensator) fails or an argument is NIHIL.
      The header promises a reason on stderr, but lib/pictor_applicatio.c
      itself prints one only when the document cannot be opened or
      created ("pictor: documentum").</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I mount pictor as one pane inside a host repository such as vicus?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_montare PictorMontatio" via="lib/vicus_applicatio.c">pictor_montare(m,
      piscina, intern, volumen, repo, id, latitudo, altitudo,
      systemata) creates the branch &lt;pictor id&gt; if absent and opens
      (or creates) the drawing stored in spatium id; id NIHIL mounts
      at the repository root, which must already be a pictor element.
      The PictorMontatio holds the contexts its registries point to,
      so give it a stable address and never copy it. systemata may be
      NIHIL (tests).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I show a different drawing in a mounted pictor pane, or create a new one?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_picturam_ponere pictor_picturam_condere pictor_documenta_enumerare">pictor_picturam_ponere(m,
      spatium) shows an existing drawing; it returns FALSUM unless the
      drawing is already in the pane's document table or listed by
      pictor_documenta_enumerare (manifest origin
      "pictor:documentum"), so a scriba document is never opened as a
      canvas. pictor_picturam_condere(m, spatium) creates a blank one
      at the pane's new-canvas size and shows it; it returns FALSUM if
      the name is empty or already listed by
      pictor_documenta_enumerare. Caution (audit 2026-10-18, unfixed):
      when the pane is a PictorApplicatio's montatio, either call leaves
      app.doc pointing at the old document, so read app.montatio.doc
      afterwards.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I keep using PictorApplicatio.doc after the shown drawing changes?
    <responsum symbolum="PictorApplicatio pictor_picturam_ponere pictor_applicatio_aedificare">No:
      despite its header comment "= montatio.doc", PictorApplicatio.doc
      is a copy taken once in pictor_applicatio_aedificare.
      pictor_picturam_ponere re-points montatio.doc and the doc of the
      action, figure and composition contexts, but not app.doc, so
      read app.montatio.doc for the drawing on screen. app.actiones and
      app.figurae stay valid: a swap changes the contexts, never the
      registries. The standalone app never swaps by itself (worklog:
      only vicus panes do).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what size does a new pictor canvas get?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_montare pictor_picturam_condere">The
      surface minus one cell (VI pixels) on each side in width, and
      minus (III status lines + II) cells of VIII pixels in height, with
      a floor of LXIV pixels each way. The surface is the latitudo and
      altitudo given to pictor_montare (kept in
      montatio.compositio.fenestra_latitudo/altitudo), so a canvas made
      later by pictor_picturam_condere uses the mount-time size even
      after the window was resized. A drawing that already exists
      keeps its own size whatever the pane size.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does PictorMontatio keep a table of documents by spatium?
    <responsum symbolum="PictorMontatio pictor_picturam_ponere" via="lib/pictor_applicatio.worklog.md">Each
      PictorDocumentum is about a megabyte of pixels plus history in
      the arena, so reopening it on every swap would leak. The table
      also guarantees one document object per drawing; vicus shares
      one table across all pictor panes so two panes on the same
      drawing write one history. The root spatium "" is stored under
      key "." because tabula_dispersa takes no empty key.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
